\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Rotating only one endpoint}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{On an edge between two distinct vertices a sign flip at the head
reverses both the head field and the link. The [joint
weight](fdip-010A) stays fixed. Flipping the sign at the vertex of a
loop changes both ends of that loop at once. Which of these changes
pairs contributions with opposite values in a sum over configurations?}
